  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 206.01 Waiver of Rules",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 206.01 Waiver of Rules.\n\n(a) The commissioner shall waive the provisions of any rule, except where precluded by statute or by Cul-H 204.04, upon request by an interested party if the committee finds that:\n\n(1) The waiver serves the public interest; and\n\n(2) The waiver will not disrupt the orderly and efficient resolution of matters before the division.\n\n(b) In determining the public interest, the commissioner shall waive a rule if:\n\n(1) Compliance with the rule would be onerous or inapplicable given the circumstances of the affected person; or\n\n(2) The purpose of the rule would be satisfied by an alternative method proposed.\n\n(c) Any interested party seeking a waiver shall make a request in writing, except as provided in (d) below.\n\n(d) The commissioner shall accept for consideration any waiver request made orally during a hearing or pre-hearing conference.\n\n(e) A request for a waiver shall specify the basis for the waiver and the proposed alternative, if any.\n\nSource. #10219, eff 10-30-12\n\nAppendix",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h200.html"
